# Importable modules, not DAG files. None of these defines a DAG.
#
# Airflow's safe-mode DAG discovery imports any .py file containing the string
# "dag" or "airflow", and every entry below mentions one or the other. That
# makes Airflow import them standalone as DAG candidates, so any failure inside
# them surfaces in the UI as a spurious DAG import error even though none
# defines a DAG -- clickhouse_utils.py imports clickhouse_connect at module
# level and can trip the dag-processor parse timeout that way.
#
# This only affects DAG *discovery* -- the modules stay importable from the
# orchestrator and transformation DAGs as normal.
#
# Matched as globs: core.dag_ignore_file_syntax is "glob" here, not regexp.
# Edits take effect only after the dag-processor restarts.
clickhouse_utils.py
egov_api_utils.py
raw_event_bronze_config.py
raw_event_bronze_processor.py
